WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.824
- [Kelly] I love your outfit.

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:02.720
- (laughs) Thank you.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.670
- Like honestly, I was
getting ready for the show

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.690
and you were rehearsing
and stuff, and I was like,

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.350
we were all talking
about your whole style.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.900
Are you really into style?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.210
- Yeah, I'm really into fashion.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.860
I've been like shifting
more towards it just lately,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.693
you know, just trying to change my--

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:17.940
- Yeah, well, you do it well.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.334
- Yeah, thank you, thank you.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.965
- Well, meet Kal, he likes
naans and sweet pickles.

00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:24.741
So yeah--
- Naans and sweet pickles.

00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:25.574
Absolutely.

00:00:25.574 --> 00:00:27.891
- Do you have any like major
obsessions that you love

00:00:27.891 --> 00:00:29.830
that you can't live without?

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.800
- Probably, I've been trying
to go like vegan lately--

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.670
- Oh, nice.
- Oh, good for you.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.524
But I've been craving steak, but I--

00:00:36.524 --> 00:00:37.357
(Kal and audience laughs)

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:40.763
- Oh, exactly, or cheese.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.870
Actually--
- It's so good for you though.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.880
Yeah, but I made a mistake, I
ate a piece of bacon yesterday

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.810
and I just didn't miss the--

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.339
- Okay, wait.
- Did it kill your stomach?

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:52.441
- Yeah--

00:00:52.441 --> 00:00:54.990
- How do you accidentally
eat a piece of bacon?

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.590
- Okay, I'ma tell you that,
it's actually a funny story

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.372
'cause, okay, so I was really hungry.

00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:03.640
I told the hotel to
bring me an egg sandwich.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.070
So when the egg sandwich got
to my room, it had bacon on it.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.300
But if I removed it,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.730
then the whole sandwich would fall apart

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.970
and I was really hungry--

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.883
- [Kelly] Yeah, you lean in.

00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:13.293
- And, I just ate, I just ate it.

00:01:13.293 --> 00:01:15.080
I was like it wouldn't hurt.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.607
- Yeah, oh, I love bacon.

00:01:17.607 --> 00:01:18.440
- It didn't hurt.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.295
- So wait, where are you from originally?

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:21.150
- I'm from Alabama.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:21.983
- Oh, a Southern boy.

00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.890
Oh, that's gotta be real
hard to give up meat.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.990
'Cause that's all we all grew up on, okay.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:27.240
Have you spent any time in Alabama?

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.073
I've toured there quite a bit.

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:30.270
- Yeah, Alabama and Mississippi,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.270
and Huntsville, Alabama,

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.600
where I went to space camp as a kid.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.310
There's a big NASA thing down there.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.510
- When you said Huntsville,
like I always think prison.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.200
I don't know for some
reason, so I was like,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.140
what were you doing there?

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.700
- Well, I went to the
NASA part of the prison.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.410
- You went to space camp,
that's so cool, okay.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.511
- [Kal] Oh, whoa.

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:50.085
- [Kelly] I love this.

00:01:50.085 --> 00:01:53.017
- Whoa, so quick. You guys are so quick.

00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:54.600
I didn't know you had that.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.480
- We are amazing, this team.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.560
We're Emmy-winning.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.086
I don't know if you know, Kal.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:00.961
(audience applauding)

00:02:00.961 --> 00:02:03.490
So I have to ask, this is crazy

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.520
because I feel like they're deadly,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.120
but I feel like you had a
pet baboon at some point.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.641
Like, is that real?
- Yeah, but--

00:02:11.641 --> 00:02:14.067
Can't they kill you?
- Wait, you had what?

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.333
I feel like they can definitely kill you.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.652
- Yeah, I found that out
like two weeks later.

00:02:19.652 --> 00:02:22.178
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:22.178 --> 00:02:23.565
I didn't know it was a baboon.

00:02:23.565 --> 00:02:24.650
- What?

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.070
Wait, what did you think it was?

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.370
- I thought it was just
a baby monkey, like...

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.470
- Where did you get it, and how did,

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.210
did it attack you?

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:35.800
- No, I adopted it from this guy

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.240
and I had it like for two weeks and then,

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.330
I was posting him on my social media

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.028
and then I read a comment
that said, that's a baboon.

00:02:44.028 --> 00:02:46.290
I was like...
(audience laughing)

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.123
Then I was like,

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.730
she can't know what she's talking about.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.772
So I Googled it, and I'm looking at this,

00:02:54.772 --> 00:02:56.800
I'm holding him, I'm
looking at the picture,

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:57.677
and I'm looking at him, I'm, like,

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.533
"It's really a baboon,
you know what I'm saying."

00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:02.004
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:02.004 --> 00:03:04.370
So, first of all, congratulations,

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.760
I love that your first song is with Drake,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.587
like (mimics disco siren), that's amazing.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.811
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.811 --> 00:03:10.710
So, you worked with Drake?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.189
- My first, my first--

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:15.440
- Not your first thing, your
first mainstream, yes, yes.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.500
I should've said that, your
first mainstream thing.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.110
But I love that, you worked with Drake

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.853
and also John Legend, who I love.

00:03:23.479 --> 00:03:25.780
I mean, he's so much fun
to sing with and work with.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.340
He's so cool and so talented.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.900
But I heard that there was a story of you

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.200
missing a FaceTime from Drake.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.490
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.170
When he first did the record,

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.210
he like FaceTimed me at like the next day

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.580
at three in the morning and I was asleep.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.844
- [Kelly] Well, of course
you are, so is the world.

00:03:41.844 --> 00:03:44.340
- (laughing) Yeah, so I
woke up in the morning,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.700
I was like, "Oh, I missed
a FaceTime from Drake."

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.200
Like I was panicking.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.390
I was like, "What if he
didn't do the song now,

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.830
you know what I'm saying?"

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.580
So I had waited the next
day, that same time at three,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.110
I stayed up all the way
to three in the morning

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.790
and FaceTimed him around the same time

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.270
and he answered.
- Oh my God.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:02.260
- Was he like in a different time zone?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.200
Is that why?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.160
- Yeah, he was in Canada.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.150
So I don't know the time difference.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.700
- Well, that's not that
big of a time difference.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.720
I'm like, oh my gosh.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.710
I don't know if I've
ever been that person.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.701
That's like rocking it at 3:00 or 4:00 AM.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:17.270
That seems like a
difficult lifestyle for me.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.940
So wait, you're playing,
your song's "Beautiful Lies"

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.030
love that title by the way.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.980
And "You're Mines Still" first
day, so what are they about?

00:04:24.977 --> 00:04:29.760
- "Beautiful Lies" is
basically about a love triangle

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.673
with someone just, you know,

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.930
leading you on, you know.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.700
It's about love, someone leading you on,

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.730
telling you beautiful lies,
things you may believe.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.390
And "You're Mines Still" is just,

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.440
you know, "You're Mines Still"

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.168
it's just toxic,

00:04:45.168 --> 00:04:46.001
just a toxic--

00:04:46.001 --> 00:04:47.519
- [Kelly] I love it. (laughs)

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.035
- One of those toxic--
(audience applauding)

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:50.185
- I love it, I love it.

